  "summary": "P1 credential phishing, Aisha Khan (HR Generalist, user_id 5, aisha.khan@brightline.example, device BL-LT-0105). Reported: clicked link in a \"payroll verification\" email and typed her password into the page. Exact click time not given (assume 9 Oct 2026). Did not mention approving a Duo push or opening an attachment. Checks: account is active, 0 failed logins, password last set 2026-09-09. Duo push enrolled on her phone. Sign-in logs for the last 14 days: 9 successful sign-ins, all from New York, US, on her usual corporate (203.0.113.10) and residential (198.51.100.25) IPs, all at 09:35 local with Duo. Latest was 2026-10-08 13:35 UTC. No hosting-network, foreign, failed, or denied-MFA sign-ins. No suspicious activity found so far, so I did NOT request a sign-in block. Quarantine shows a phishing message Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example (lookalike domain, capital I in place of l), subject \"Urgent: verify your payroll login\", received 2026-10-09 08:29 UTC. A copy probably reached her inbox or another delivery path. It is not releasable and was not released. Actions: password reset queued (approval #1). The tech must verify her by callback to the number on file and give her the temp password by phone. Still needed: confirm the click time, check whether other users got the same lookalike-domain email (possible campaign), purge it from mailboxes, block the domain/URL, keep watching sign-ins/mailbox rules after the click, and block sign-in if anything suspicious shows up.",
